Priya's ./config.jet before, and the identical edit every archetype below produces when she installs Inkscape -- this diff is the reproducibility guarantee, the same no matter which UX wins:

  module halcyon {
      sources: {
          core: path@./jet-pkgs,
+         apps: nixpkgs@stable,
      }
      system.halcyon: {
          target: linux.x64,
          options: [
-             user.priya.packages: [core.hello],
+             user.priya.packages: [core.hello, apps.inkscape],
          ],
      }
  }

Then the profile engine runs `jetos user switch priya` (D-JOS-USERAPPLY1): builds a new generation, switches it in, rollback available. Uninstall deletes the apps.inkscape token. Live state is never touched directly -- the file is always the truth.

