The x86 and portable files have the same signature, input, output, and printed `Product128{low: 21, high: 0}` result.

For x86 source plus x86 target, only that selected closure parses, checks, and emits. The portable file is absent unless imported. For portable source plus any supported target, only that closure parses, checks, and emits. For x86 source plus aarch64 or wasm32, common checks run and the selected assembly receives a target diagnostic before generation. An absent file is not parsed and cannot cause that diagnostic.

B has no automatic cross-target dispatch or host fallback. It preserves current syntax but makes callers maintain source partitions.

