After the final disconnect, the Nest-only observer should settle at connections 0 and pending 0. The source explicitly aborts connection-owned fetches and removes their map entries.

This is source reasoning, not a measured cleanup result. For A/B/C, observe equivalent resource release without requiring the Nest-only HTTP counter endpoint.

For the failure boundary, disconnect after the ledger commits but before the acknowledgement reaches the client. Its callback timeout means completion is unknown, not rolled back.

An explicit later reconnect and same-id emission can return the existing receipt. The shown client does not automatically retry a failed or uncertain call.

